            "correct_answer": "$\\sigma>0$, and the integral equals $\\dfrac{2}{\\sigma+j\\omega}$.",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Combine the exponential factors to get $2e^{-(\\sigma+j\\omega)t}$. The oscillatory factor has unit magnitude, so convergence on $[0,\\infty)$ is controlled by $e^{-\\sigma t}$, which requires $\\sigma>0$.",
